<item>
            <title>[LU-20645] &apos;lfs getstripe --printf&apos; to print specific fields from layout</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20645</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;It would be useful to have an &quot;&lt;tt&gt;lfs getstripe &lt;b&gt;--printf &lt;em&gt;FORMAT&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;em&gt;FILE&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/tt&gt;&quot; option to print specific fields from a file&apos;s layout.  There is already &quot;&lt;tt&gt;lfs find --printf &lt;em&gt;FORMAT&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/tt&gt;&quot; that can print all of the useful fields, but it needs to be connected to &lt;tt&gt;getstripe&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
